# What `docker build` is allowed to see.
#
# This file is an ALLOWLIST — `*` drops the whole tree and the `!` lines add back
# exactly what the Dockerfile copies. Written that way for one reason:
# `src/rya/console/dist/` is a gitignored BUILD OUTPUT that lives inside a directory
# the image needs (`COPY src ./src`). A developer who has run `npm run build` locally
# has a `dist/` in their working tree, and without this file that stale, unversioned
# bundle gets baked into the image and silently overrides the one the console builder
# stage produces. The image would then differ from machine to machine while the
# Dockerfile stayed identical — which is exactly the failure that is hardest to
# believe when you hit it.
#
# The allowlist buys three more things:
#   - `.env` cannot leak into an image layer even if a later COPY gets careless;
#   - `.venv/`, `.git/` and `.rya/` stop being uploaded to the daemon on every build
#     (hundreds of MB of context for a build that reads none of it);
#   - adding a COPY without updating this file fails loudly at build time instead of
#     quietly shipping something unintended.
#
# Adding a COPY to the Dockerfile? Add its path here too.

*

# The Python distribution metadata. `pyproject.toml` declares
# `license-files = ["LICENSE"]` and `readme = "README.md"`; hatchling reads both
# during `pip install .`, so neither is optional.
!pyproject.toml
!README.md
!LICENSE

# The platform itself.
!src

# The console source, compiled by the `console` builder stage.
!web/console

# --- re-exclusions inside the allowed paths ------------------------------------

# The whole point of this file. Built by the `console` stage, never copied from the
# host. See docs/PACKAGING.md.
src/rya/console/dist

# 100+ MB of host-resolved dependencies, most of them platform-specific. The builder
# stage runs its own `npm ci` from the lockfile.
web/console/node_modules
web/console/.vite
web/console/vite.config.ts.timestamp-*

# Byte-compiled and cached artefacts from the host's interpreter, which is not
# necessarily the image's.
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/*.egg-info
